While rather limited, there is still enough to do and see in its current state to keep you interested. More trucks and content are on the way, and SCS does a good job of keeping their games updated. For the $20 price tag it's very competitive.
Things it does well;
A closer to reality economy vs ETS2 while still having high enough revenue jobs to keep you growing and engaged. Observence of American traffic laws and trucking regulations, including a somewhat limited simulation of cargo weight regulations and an incorporation of weigh stations, as well as vehicle insurance.
Areas of improvement;
We don't drive around in 50s cars everywhere. I know they were trying to grasp and incorporate all the Americana they could, and it's nice to see it every once in awhile, but it's just rather silly. Also the AI is quite frankly rather dimwitted and contributes to unnecessary congestion.

